{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Go for yourself</b>. HaShem commanded Abraham while he was still in Ur of the Chaldeans that he should leave his land and his birthplace and also his father's house. The reason is that HaShem knew that Terah, after he set out for the land of Canaan, settled in Haran, and Terah did not die until sixty years after Abraham left his father's house from Haran. Only the verse did not specify his age when he left Ur of the Chaldeans. And after it says \"which I will show you,\" He revealed to him the sod, for thus it is written: \"and they set out to go to the land of Canaan\" (Genesis 12:5). Or the meaning of \"I will show you\" may be what He said to him: \"for all the land that you see, to you I will give it\" (Genesis 13:15)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:44:14.840216850Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}